Software Requirements Specification (SRS)
Skill Swap – A Peer-to-Peer Skill Exchange Platform

Version 1.0

1. Introduction

Purpose

The purpose of the Skill Swap application is to provide a platform where users can exchange skills and knowledge without monetary transactions. 
The system enables users to showcase the skills they can teach and discover others from whom they can learn. 
This project focuses on frontend development and demonstrates a modern, responsive user interface.

Scope

Skill Swap is a frontend web application designed to:
* Allow users to create and manage profiles.
* Display skills users can offer and skills they want to learn.
* Search and filter available skills.
* Simulate sending and receiving skill swap requests.
* Store data using Local Storage or mock JSON data.

Objectives

* Promote peer-to-peer learning.
* Provide a user-friendly interface.
* Demonstrate frontend development concepts.
* Build a responsive web application.


2. Overall Description

Product Perspective

Skill Swap is a standalone frontend application.
It does not require a backend server or database. 
User data is stored locally within the browser.

Product Functions

The application allows users to:

* Register (UI only)
* Log in (UI only)
* Create a profile
* Add offered skills
* Add desired skills
* Browse available users
* Search skills
* Filter skills by category
* Send swap requests
* Accept or reject requests (simulated)
* View current swaps
* Edit profile information

User Classes

User

* Register account (UI)
* Update profile
* Browse skills
* Search users
* Request skill exchange
* Manage requests



3. Functional Requirements

FR1: User Registration

* Display registration form.
* Validate required fields.
* Save data locally.

FR2: User Login

* Display login page.
* Authenticate using Local Storage (simulation).

FR3: User Profile

Users can:
* Upload profile image (optional)
* Enter name
* Bio
* Location
* Offered skills
* Skills to learn

FR4: Skill Management

Users can:
* Add new skills
* Edit skills
* Delete skills

FR5: Browse Skills

Display:
* User name
* Skill offered
* Skill wanted
* Category

FR6: Search

Allow searching by:
* Skill name
* User name
* Category

FR7: Filter

Filter skills using:
* Technology
* Language
* Music
* Design
* Fitness
* Business
* Others

FR8: Swap Request

Users can:
* Send request
* Accept request
* Reject request
* Cancel request

(All actions are simulated on the frontend.)

FR9: Dashboard

Display:

* Active requests
* Completed swaps
* Profile summary



4. Non-Functional Requirements

Performance:

* Load pages within 2 seconds.
* Fast search functionality.

Reliability:

* Store user data safely in Local Storage.
* Prevent data loss during navigation.

Usability:

* Clean and intuitive interface.
* Easy navigation.
* Mobile-friendly layout.

Security:

* Basic client-side validation.
* Password masking in the UI.
* No sensitive information stored online.

Maintainability:

* Modular code structure.
* Reusable components.
* Clear comments.

Compatibility:

Supports:

* Google Chrome
* Mozilla Firefox
* Microsoft Edge
* Safari



